1
00:01:20,727 --> 00:01:27,189
In sha Allah ho Ta'ala(إن شاء الله), this will be our last session on the life of our great leader,

2
00:01:27,346 --> 00:01:32,488
 Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه و رضي الله عن الصّحابة أجمعين .

3
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:44,385
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, as we know and seen by going through his biography,

4
00:01:44,822 --> 00:01:47,279
 was very strict in his rules.

5
00:01:48,114 --> 00:01:57,930
Umar bin Khattab رضي الله عنه wanted Madina to be pure and clean from all of the contaminations,

6
00:01:58,009 --> 00:02:03,597
if we would call it, that were occurring in the periphery of the Islamic world,

7
00:02:04,007 --> 00:02:05,793
where people were just embracing Islam

8
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:08,483
and where you had Ahl-Uz-Zimmah(أهل الذمه) and non Muslims.

9
00:02:08,717 --> 00:02:10,133
It was a blend and a mixture.

10
00:02:10,194 --> 00:02:13,368
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted Madina to be far away from that.

11
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:22,963
Therefore, he did not want to have, any non Muslim slaves in Madina.

12
00:02:23,425 --> 00:02:27,949
Now, obviously, non Muslim freemen, were not allowed in Madina to start with,

13
00:02:28,402 --> 00:02:30,618
based on the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ of,

14
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:33,414
أَخْرِجُ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ مِنْ جَزِيْرَةِ الْعَرَبْ

15
00:02:33,793 --> 00:02:37,057
 Drive the Mushrikeen(مشركين) out of the Arabian Peninsula, and Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

16
00:02:37,082 --> 00:02:38,461
لَا يَجْتَمِعْ فِيْهَا دِيْنَانْ

17
00:02:38,793 --> 00:02:42,250
No two religions should be combined in Arabia.

18
00:02:43,059 --> 00:02:51,713
However, since slaves, do not have free choice and they are part of the property,

19
00:02:52,268 --> 00:02:56,644
they were not seen as a violation of this rule of Hadith(حديث).

20
00:02:56,987 --> 00:03:01,215
However, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn't comfortable having them in Madina,

21
00:03:02,521 --> 00:03:07,126
and by the way, we will mention the word slaves and slavery here.

22
00:03:08,802 --> 00:03:14,495
Unfortunately, the word today, doesn't mean, what it meant to the Sahabah(صحابه) yesterday.

23
00:03:15,711 --> 00:03:20,301
Slavery in the European context was based on racism.

24
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:24,621
It was one color enslaving another.

25
00:03:25,979 --> 00:03:27,994
And that's a completely different concept

26
00:03:28,019 --> 00:03:31,606
than the slavery that existed in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه).

27
00:03:33,151 --> 00:03:35,163
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ and Sahabah(صحابه),

28
00:03:35,237 --> 00:03:38,799
they were living by international law that existed, of the time,

29
00:03:39,035 --> 00:03:42,134
 and that is that prisoners of war become slaves,

30
00:03:42,316 --> 00:03:45,411
no matter what their color is, what their background is,

31
00:03:45,633 --> 00:03:47,110
Arabs can be slaves,

32
00:03:47,419 --> 00:03:52,517
Africans can be slaves, European can be slaves, Persian can be slaves

33
00:03:53,336 --> 00:03:57,245
and that was something at least around Arabia,

34
00:03:57,323 --> 00:04:00,241
that was how the situation was with the Roman and Persian Empire.

35
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,645
However, the difference was that

36
00:04:04,919 --> 00:04:10,257
other people or other religions were enslaving people and we're very brutal in their slavery.

37
00:04:10,282 --> 00:04:21,138
However in Islam, slavery was just like a job, and it was a very accommodating job.

38
00:04:22,142 --> 00:04:26,701
So the slaves would have to eat from the same food that the master eats.

39
00:04:28,804 --> 00:04:37,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want the slaves to be separated from the eating places of the free men,

40
00:04:37,882 --> 00:04:39,574
so they would eat all together.

41
00:04:40,428 --> 00:04:42,964
It's not like you have separate quarters for the slaves where they eat,

42
00:04:43,257 --> 00:04:44,979
and then the Freeman eat in a different place.

43
00:04:45,019 --> 00:04:46,543
No! They would eat together.

44
00:04:47,217 --> 00:04:51,577
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not allow, disciplining them brutally

45
00:04:53,195 --> 00:04:55,513
and they need to be treated with compassion.

46
00:04:55,553 --> 00:04:58,020
Rasool Allah ﷺ  said: They are your brothers.

47
00:04:58,879 --> 00:05:02,303
In fact, Rasool Allah ﷺ before he passes away,

48
00:05:02,715 --> 00:05:05,188
his last advice to the Ummah(امة) was?

49
00:05:07,368 --> 00:05:10,668
Salah(صلاة) and be kind to your slaves.

50
00:05:10,975 --> 00:05:14,944
 أَلصَّلَاةْ ، وَمَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ

51
00:05:15,507 --> 00:05:17,554
This was his last advice to the Ummah(امة).

52
00:05:19,935 --> 00:05:22,002
So, they are treated very well and

53
00:05:23,266 --> 00:05:27,795
because of this good treatment and because they had free opportunity, like everybody else,

54
00:05:29,527 --> 00:05:35,506
slaves many of them became scholars, many of them became army generals.

55
00:05:38,217 --> 00:05:42,232
Possibly Tariq Bin Ziyad(طارق بن زياد) was a slave and he was the one opened Andalus(ألأندلس) .

56
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:52,386
Attaa(عطاء) was a former slave and he was considered to be the greatest scholar of Makkah(مكه)

57
00:05:52,525 --> 00:05:54,803
in his time, in the era of a At-Tabaeen(ألتابعين).

58
00:05:56,967 --> 00:05:59,560
Nafea(نافع) who was the salve of Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر).

59
00:06:00,404 --> 00:06:03,131
He was the carrier of the knowledge of Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر),

60
00:06:03,155 --> 00:06:05,061
he was a transmitter of that knowledge.

61
00:06:06,266 --> 00:06:10,071
What is referred to as the golden chain of narration in Hadith(حديث)

62
00:06:10,414 --> 00:06:11,060
is Malik(مالك),

63
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,084
An(عن) Nafie(النافع),

64
00:06:12,164 --> 00:06:13,227
Ann(عن) Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر)

65
00:06:13,307 --> 00:06:14,283
Ann(عن) Rasool Ullah

66
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:18,596
Imam Malik(إمام مالك) was his An-Nafea(النافع) student, by the way,

67
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,381
Imam Malik(إمام مالك) was a student of the slave.

68
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:26,120
This golden chain of narration is Malik(مالك) narrating from An-Nafea(النافع),

69
00:06:26,144 --> 00:06:29,254
narrating from Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر), narrating from Rasool Allah ﷺ,

70
00:06:30,254 --> 00:06:32,746
and there's some Ahadith(احاديث) where Ash-Shafie(أشافعي),

71
00:06:33,582 --> 00:06:35,207
because Ash-Shafie(أشافعي) was a student of Malik(مالك),

72
00:06:35,261 --> 00:06:37,005
and Ahmad(أحمد) was a student of Ash-Shafie(أشافعي),

73
00:06:37,211 --> 00:06:38,489
 you have some Ahadith(احاديث),

74
00:06:39,448 --> 00:06:41,944
Ahmad(أحمد) narrating from Ash-Shafie(أشافعي), narrating from Malik(مالك),

75
00:06:41,969 --> 00:06:45,068
narrating from An-Nafea(النافع), narrating from Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر).

76
00:06:45,092 --> 00:06:47,295
So, you can add more gold to that chain.

77
00:06:48,690 --> 00:06:53,948
So, don't carry the same connotations of slavery today

78
00:06:54,235 --> 00:06:59,353
 and apply them to slavery yesterday, it was a completely different thing.

79
00:07:00,734 --> 00:07:05,408
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want these slaves, who were taken in war.

80
00:07:06,453 --> 00:07:07,882
He did not want them in Madina.

81
00:07:10,168 --> 00:07:15,312
However, some of Sahabah(صحابه) were lobbying for having them in Madina,

82
00:07:15,504 --> 00:07:18,719
 because they were the basis for their business.

83
00:07:19,832 --> 00:07:22,176
And Al-Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبدالمطلب) was one of them.

84
00:07:22,465 --> 00:07:27,114
And he had the most slaves in Madina and it was an income generating thing for him.

85
00:07:27,598 --> 00:07:32,119
So, he was lobbying Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه to allow them into Madina

86
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:37,223
and Umar(عُمَر), because of the pressure of the Sahabah(صحابه) agreed to have them in Madina.

87
00:07:40,745 --> 00:07:45,066
 One of these slaves, he's Persian from Faris(فارس)

88
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:54,182
he was good in making stone Mills, he was a good skilled worker.

89
00:07:58,323 --> 00:08:03,997
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه was approached by this man, his name is Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ).

90
00:08:06,192 --> 00:08:12,660
He told Umar(عُمَر): My master Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبه) is charging me too much.

91
00:08:13,552 --> 00:08:19,066
So, this man would work and Al-Mugheera(ألمغيره) would take part of the profits.

92
00:08:21,573 --> 00:08:25,767
So, can you ask him to reduce my payments.

93
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:28,123
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

94
00:08:28,192 --> 00:08:30,340
إِتَّقِى اللهَ وَأَحْسِنْ إِلَى مَوْلآكْ

95
00:08:30,568 --> 00:08:32,635
Fear Allah and be good towards your master.

96
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:39,221
So, this man turned around and he said to himself.

97
00:08:41,665 --> 00:08:48,283
يَسَعُ النَّاسَ عَدْلُه’ غَيْرِيْ أكُلٌ النَاسِ يَسْعَهُمْ عَدْلُه’ إلَّا أنَا

98
00:08:49,158 --> 00:08:52,972
His justice is sufficient for everyone except me.

99
00:08:54,036 --> 00:08:56,336
He is just with everyone except myself.

100
00:08:57,551 --> 00:08:59,540
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him that,

101
00:09:00,012 --> 00:09:03,953
with the intention of going to Al-Mugheera(ألمغيره) and asking him to reduce the payments.

102
00:09:04,582 --> 00:09:07,480
But that was the way of Umar(عُمَر) he would give advice to both sides.

103
00:09:08,414 --> 00:09:10,918
but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not tell him, Well I'm going to go to Al-Mugheera(ألمغيره),

104
00:09:11,352 --> 00:09:13,547
 he just told them, fear Allah and be good to your master.

105
00:09:13,945 --> 00:09:15,302
And then he went to Al-Mugheera(ألمغيره)

106
00:09:15,364 --> 00:09:18,960
and he told Al-Mugheera(ألمغيره) to reduce the payments on Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ).

107
00:09:20,177 --> 00:09:27,101
But Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ) has already made the intentions of killing Umar(عُمَر)

108
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:35,671
and since he was a good skilled worker, he carved out this dagger, which was double edged.

109
00:09:36,691 --> 00:09:42,746
So, you have the handle and then you have the blade pointing from both sides.

110
00:09:43,074 --> 00:09:44,990
So, it could strike both ways.

111
00:09:46,228 --> 00:09:51,840
And it was very well done and then he soaked it in poison,

112
00:09:52,357 --> 00:09:54,677
until it absorbed all of the poison.

113
00:09:58,372 --> 00:10:00,948
Apparently, he went to Hurmozaan(هرموزان) and he asked him,

114
00:10:01,009 --> 00:10:02,508
what do you think about this dagger? He said;

115
00:10:02,735 --> 00:10:05,152
This dagger, if it touches anyone, it would kill him.

116
00:10:08,769 --> 00:10:12,675
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) passes next to him and he said;

117
00:10:13,956 --> 00:10:22,120
I heard that you are able to make a mill that works on wind, a windmill.

118
00:10:24,136 --> 00:10:25,498
He said: Yes, I do.

119
00:10:26,654 --> 00:10:30,910
And I'm going to make you a mill that everyone in the world would hear about.

120
00:10:33,185 --> 00:10:35,434
Mean I'm gonna grind you on that mill.

121
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:40,508
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) left him and he went and he said;

122
00:10:41,243 --> 00:10:42,514
"تَوَّا عَدْنِ الْعَبْدََ"

123
00:10:42,983 --> 00:10:48,031
The slave has threatened me, but he did nothing about it.

124
00:10:49,730 --> 00:10:52,427
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn't worried about dying.

125
00:10:53,446 --> 00:10:55,211
He didn't care about his personal safety,

126
00:10:55,236 --> 00:10:58,641
he would care about the orphans and the woman of Iraq,

127
00:10:58,666 --> 00:11:00,273
but he wouldn't care about his own safety.

128
00:11:01,348 --> 00:11:02,476
So, he did nothing about it.

129
00:11:03,164 --> 00:11:08,102
He did not have any bodyguards, before that, or after that.

130
00:11:12,402 --> 00:11:17,058
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه would enter into the Masjid(مسجد)

131
00:11:17,083 --> 00:11:20,015
and he would straighten the lines saying Istawoo(إستؤو)

132
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,824
and he would straighten them with his hand.

133
00:11:26,157 --> 00:11:28,456
Amr Bin Maimoom(عمروبن ميمون) and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) he said;

134
00:11:28,595 --> 00:11:32,293
Nobody was between me and Umar in Salaat-Ul-Fajr(صلاةالفجر) but Abdullah Bin Abbas(عبدالله بن عباس)

135
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:37,032
meaning he was in the second row right behind Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

136
00:11:37,079 --> 00:11:38,870
between him and Umar(عُمَر) is Abdullah Bin Abbas(عبدالله بن عباس).

137
00:11:41,710 --> 00:11:45,996
And he said: Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه would recite the long Surah(سورة) in the first Rakay(ركاة)

138
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:47,472
until the people gathered.

139
00:11:49,452 --> 00:11:52,154
So, he would recite Surat-Al-Nakhl(سورةالنخل) or Surah-Yusuf(سورةيوسف)

140
00:11:52,592 --> 00:11:53,967
or some similar Surah(سورة).

141
00:11:55,904 --> 00:11:59,453
He said: As soon as Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said: Allah Ho Akbar(الله أكبر),

142
00:12:00,806 --> 00:12:06,794
Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ) attacked him from behind and stabbed him on his shoulders

143
00:12:07,673 --> 00:12:11,755
and then he stabbed him again in his waist and that was the one that killed him.

144
00:12:13,544 --> 00:12:15,238
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), He said;

145
00:12:15,298 --> 00:12:17,317
"أكَلَنِ الْكَلْبْ، أوْقَتَلَنِ الْكَلْبَ"

146
00:12:17,677 --> 00:12:21,649
The dog has eaten me, or the dog has killed me.

147
00:12:23,396 --> 00:12:25,950
That was the first statement that he made,

148
00:12:25,974 --> 00:12:26,820
"أوْقَتَلَنِ الْكَلْبَ .."

149
00:12:26,918 --> 00:12:29,846
The dog has killed me and he doesn't know who it is.

150
00:12:32,205 --> 00:12:36,577
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was struck, was stabbed twice

151
00:12:38,127 --> 00:12:40,619
and then Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ) went on a killing rampage.

152
00:12:40,982 --> 00:12:43,297
Whoever, he would see in front of him, he would stab him.

153
00:12:44,717 --> 00:12:47,868
So, he stabbed 13 people, seven of them died.

154
00:12:49,401 --> 00:12:52,178
And then, one of the Sahabah(صحابه), obviously, they were not armed and the Masjid(مسجد),

155
00:12:52,202 --> 00:12:55,609
they weren't carrying their weapons, there were no security guards,

156
00:12:56,089 --> 00:12:58,979
the Khalifah رضي الله عنه would come in without any guards.

157
00:13:00,513 --> 00:13:01,807
So, one of the Sahabah(صحابه) what he did.

158
00:13:01,847 --> 00:13:05,061
He threw a Thaub(ثوب) a cloth, over him.

159
00:13:06,310 --> 00:13:09,356
When Abu Lulu'u(أبولولؤ) knew that he would be arrested.

160
00:13:09,958 --> 00:13:12,920
He slaughtered himself and he committed suicide.

161
00:13:14,918 --> 00:13:20,252
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, He held the hand of Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) who was behind him,

162
00:13:20,609 --> 00:13:25,940
 and he pulled him to the Mihraab(محراب) to lead the Salah(صلاة)

163
00:13:26,561 --> 00:13:32,350
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه , is the one who led the Salah(صلاة) and he made the very short Salah(صلاة).

164
00:13:32,938 --> 00:13:34,505
Now, Amr Bin Maimoon(عمروبن معمون) said;

165
00:13:36,018 --> 00:13:38,219
We were there and we saw what happened,

166
00:13:39,955 --> 00:13:42,510
 while the rest of the Masjid(مسجد) didn't know, what was going on.

167
00:13:42,596 --> 00:13:45,571
So, when Umar(عُمَر) went quiet, they started saying,

168
00:13:45,596 --> 00:13:47,616
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

169
00:13:48,636 --> 00:13:49,964
They didn't know what was happening.

170
00:13:50,714 --> 00:13:53,554
And then Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) stepped in and he finished the Salah(صلاة).

171
00:13:53,579 --> 00:13:54,546
And he made a very short Salah(صلاة),

172
00:13:54,586 --> 00:13:55,727
the Salah(صلاة) was very short,

173
00:13:55,936 --> 00:13:59,586
unusual for Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاةالفجر) which was very long in time of the Sahabah(صحابه),

174
00:13:59,810 --> 00:14:01,731
they would come out and it's already light.

175
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:07,204
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was carried away.

176
00:14:07,896 --> 00:14:10,685
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the first thing he did, he asked Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس)

177
00:14:11,088 --> 00:14:13,970
to go and see, who is the one who stabbed him.?

178
00:14:15,962 --> 00:14:19,193
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) went and he came back and he said;

179
00:14:19,588 --> 00:14:22,117
It was the slave of al-Mugheera Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبه).

180
00:14:22,514 --> 00:14:24,126
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

181
00:14:24,150 --> 00:14:24,960
"قَاتَلَهُ الله"

182
00:14:24,988 --> 00:14:25,871
May Allah kill him,

183
00:14:26,171 --> 00:14:28,370
I was good towards him. I did him a favor,

184
00:14:29,561 --> 00:14:33,607
he interceded on his behalf to have the payments reduced on him

185
00:14:34,942 --> 00:14:36,309
and then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

186
00:14:36,334 --> 00:14:41,141
ألحمد لله ألَّذي لَمْ يَجْعَل مِيْتَ تِيْ عَلى رَجُلٍ يَدَّعِ الّإسْلَام

187
00:14:41,825 --> 00:14:47,316
Praise be to Allah, who did not make me die, on the hands of somebody who claims to be a Muslim,

188
00:14:48,794 --> 00:14:52,960
Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدالله) that the one who killed me, is the disbelievers, a Kafir(كافر)

189
00:14:53,719 --> 00:14:57,049
because, I don't want somebody to come on the Day of Judgment arguing with me using

190
00:14:57,101 --> 00:14:57,869
لا إله إلله

191
00:14:59,965 --> 00:15:00,742
and then he said;

192
00:15:00,976 --> 00:15:08,124
لَقَدْ كُنْتَ أنْتَ وَأبُوكْ تُحِبَّانْ أنْ يَكْثُرْ أَلْعَبِيْدْ فِيْ الّمَدِيْنَه

193
00:15:08,506 --> 00:15:09,712
You and your father ....

194
00:15:09,865 --> 00:15:11,509
"أَنْ يَكْثُرُ ألْعَلُوْجْ فِي الّمَدِيْنَه"

195
00:15:11,633 --> 00:15:18,047
You and your father, wanted there to be a lot of disbelievers in Madina.

196
00:15:18,072 --> 00:15:19,423
 He's referring to these slaves.

197
00:15:20,175 --> 00:15:23,123
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: If you want, we will kill them.

198
00:15:24,107 --> 00:15:26,333
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No! You're not going to kill them,

199
00:15:26,536 --> 00:15:29,379
after they learned your language and they prayed your Salah(صلاة)

200
00:15:29,551 --> 00:15:30,763
and they make Hajj(حَجْ) with you.

201
00:15:31,341 --> 00:15:34,216
Now, you want to kill them after many of them already embraced Islam.

202
00:15:40,387 --> 00:15:45,746
So, this is, what happened in the Masjid(مسجد), with Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

203
00:15:46,058 --> 00:15:48,555
that is how he was stabbed.

204
00:15:48,626 --> 00:15:55,858
Now, they gave Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) milk to drink

205
00:15:56,953 --> 00:15:59,335
and the milk came out from his injury.

206
00:16:00,113 --> 00:16:01,276
"فَعَلِمُوْ أنَه’ مَيِّتْ"

207
00:16:01,348 --> 00:16:02,557
They knew that he's gonna die.

208
00:16:03,081 --> 00:16:07,468
That's it, there's so much internal damage, that his stomach cannot hold food

209
00:16:08,406 --> 00:16:09,675
and they knew that he's going to die.

210
00:16:10,906 --> 00:16:17,194
So, they're all now, planning for that

211
00:16:17,666 --> 00:16:21,849
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) has already given his instructions regarding the Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

212
00:16:22,182 --> 00:16:28,322
That it's the Council of six, as we mentioned last night in the dream that he saw,

213
00:16:28,932 --> 00:16:31,122
he appointed the Council of six

214
00:16:31,408 --> 00:16:33,980
Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه,

215
00:16:34,903 --> 00:16:36,113
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

216
00:16:37,227 --> 00:16:38,703
Sa'ad Bin Abi Waqas(سعدبن أبي وقاص),

217
00:16:39,481 --> 00:16:40,973
Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

218
00:16:41,608 --> 00:16:43,290
Talha Bin Obaidellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله)

219
00:16:43,562 --> 00:16:44,872
and Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام).

220
00:16:45,576 --> 00:16:50,478
And all of the six are among the 10, who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

221
00:16:51,663 --> 00:16:58,152
The only one of the 10, who was in Madina and was excluded from the group

222
00:16:58,408 --> 00:16:59,764
was Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد),

223
00:17:00,137 --> 00:17:00,864
why?

224
00:17:00,954 --> 00:17:02,977
Because he was from the clan of  Bannu Udae(بنوعدي),

225
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:04,137
the clan of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

226
00:17:04,903 --> 00:17:06,747
Because he was from his clan, he excluded him.

227
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:11,265
People were asking him to include Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر).

228
00:17:11,926 --> 00:17:13,374
Once somebody, came to him and said;

229
00:17:13,399 --> 00:17:16,542
You should give the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) to Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر),

230
00:17:17,350 --> 00:17:18,971
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) responded and said,

231
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:21,502
you're not, you're not doing that for the sake of Allah,

232
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,382
you are not saying that for the sake of Allah.

233
00:17:26,526 --> 00:17:28,326
So, these six are the council.

234
00:17:29,223 --> 00:17:31,915
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) gave them his clear instructions,

235
00:17:33,584 --> 00:17:39,972
he said: They gather in a house, for a maximum period of three days

236
00:17:41,035 --> 00:17:45,322
and they deliberate, the issue among them and choose one from among them.

237
00:17:45,347 --> 00:17:47,046
They cannot choose somebody, from outside.

238
00:17:47,284 --> 00:17:49,701
It has to be one of these six. He said;

239
00:17:49,725 --> 00:17:53,841
ألَذِيْنَ تُوُفِّيَّ أنْهُمْ الرَسُوْل وَهُوَ عَنْهُمْ رَاضِيْ

240
00:17:54,108 --> 00:17:58,946
These are the six whom, the Messenger of Allah is pleased with when he died,

241
00:17:59,507 --> 00:18:00,854
so it has to be one of the six.

242
00:18:02,334 --> 00:18:07,694
He said: Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر), can attend with them,

243
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:15,420
but he has no right, to be part of the council.

244
00:18:16,605 --> 00:18:19,055
And he said: He only attends,

245
00:18:19,551 --> 00:18:27,505
in case, you split three and three then you take his opinion, to outweigh the scale.

246
00:18:28,091 --> 00:18:32,446
So, Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) his role is, if they have split and even split,

247
00:18:32,630 --> 00:18:36,129
then his voice would count as seventh.

248
00:18:37,524 --> 00:18:43,027
And he also said: Follow the advice of Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

249
00:18:43,410 --> 00:18:45,492
because he said about him.

250
00:18:45,762 --> 00:18:49,922
رَشِيْدٌ مُسَدَّدْ لَهُمْ مِنَ اللهِ حَافِظْ فَسْمَعُ مِنْه’

251
00:18:50,934 --> 00:18:53,442
He said: Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) is a wise man,

252
00:18:54,189 --> 00:18:58,872
who has a clear vision and he is supported by a Hafiz(حافظ) from Allah,

253
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,714
he is protected by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

254
00:19:01,801 --> 00:19:04,037
 So, listen to him, listen to him.

255
00:19:04,061 --> 00:19:07,187
Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was one of the closest advisors of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

256
00:19:07,435 --> 00:19:11,610
and Umar(عُمَر) used to consider him to have a special mind and ability

257
00:19:11,739 --> 00:19:16,356
because of some insight, which Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is giving him, it is a Hafiz(حافظ) from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

258
00:19:18,577 --> 00:19:24,242
Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) is the man whom, they say he can turn rocks into gold.

259
00:19:29,738 --> 00:19:32,710
He was by far the wealthiest among the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

260
00:19:38,076 --> 00:19:42,349
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) appointed Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), Abu Talha Al-Ansaari(أبو طلحه ألأنصاري),

261
00:19:42,888 --> 00:19:45,986
to had a group of 50 men, strong men from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), he said;

262
00:19:47,706 --> 00:19:57,097
When this group appoint the Khalifah(خليفه) among them, if anyone descends, cut off their heads.

263
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:00,846
He told Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), he said;

264
00:20:00,967 --> 00:20:03,592
Ansaar(ألأنصار) are the ones, who gave victory to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

265
00:20:03,856 --> 00:20:06,694
they are the ones, who will give victory to the Khalifah(خليفه)

266
00:20:07,015 --> 00:20:11,478
and if anyone descends, I give you, my orders and commands to behead them.

267
00:20:18,724 --> 00:20:27,248
The Sahabah(صحابه) would come in, for example Hafsa(حفصه) the daughter of Umar(عُمَر) was crying

268
00:20:28,724 --> 00:20:30,965
 and she was praising her father,

269
00:20:31,804 --> 00:20:34,558
Umm-Ul-Mo'mimeen(أم مؤمنين), Hafsa(حفصه), she was praising her father,

270
00:20:35,508 --> 00:20:36,715
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told her,

271
00:20:36,755 --> 00:20:42,743
I ask you in the name of the duties that you have towards me,

272
00:20:43,852 --> 00:20:50,550
 not to speak about me like that but I cannot control your eyes.

273
00:20:51,354 --> 00:20:53,387
I do not want you to say that about me,

274
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,164
she was going on praising him.

275
00:20:55,204 --> 00:20:57,178
He said: I don't want you to say that about me.

276
00:20:57,202 --> 00:20:58,653
However, your eyes, I can't control them,

277
00:20:59,059 --> 00:21:01,446
if you want to cry, I cannot prevent you, from doing that.

278
00:21:02,091 --> 00:21:03,697
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want people to be flattered

279
00:21:03,721 --> 00:21:05,032
he didnot wanted people to praise him.

280
00:21:06,855 --> 00:21:10,604
Now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very worried

281
00:21:10,733 --> 00:21:16,753
and apparently, it was visible that he was worried, he was very concerned.

282
00:21:18,951 --> 00:21:23,102
So Abdullah Bin Abbas(عبدالله بن عباس) and some of the Sahabah(صحابه) were coming to Sooth Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

283
00:21:23,221 --> 00:21:25,864
and to comfort him.

284
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:30,854
So, Abdullah Bin Abbas رضي الله عنه came and he told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

285
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:36,584
أبْشِرْ بِالْجَنَّةْ يا أمير المومنين، أسْلَمْتَ هَيْنَ كَفَرِ النَّاسْ

286
00:21:36,851 --> 00:21:40,903
وَجَاهَدْتَ مَعَ رسول الله صلى الله على وسلم هِيْنَ خَزَلَه النَّاسْ

287
00:21:41,463 --> 00:21:45,097
وَقُبِضَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَهُوَ عَنْكَ رَاضِى ،

288
00:21:45,547 --> 00:21:51,035
 وَلَمْ يَخْتَلِفْ فِيْ خِّلَافَتِكَ أثْنَانْ، وَقُتِلْتَ شَهِيْدًا

289
00:21:52,338 --> 00:21:58,192
He said: Rejoice with paradise, you became a Muslim when people were Kuffar(كفار)

290
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,909
 and you made Jihad(جهاد) with Rasool Allah ﷺ

291
00:22:01,124 --> 00:22:03,312
when people were betraying him, and forsaking him

292
00:22:04,294 --> 00:22:07,667
and Rasool Allah ﷺ died and he was pleased with you

293
00:22:07,985 --> 00:22:10,301
and you are now killed as a Shaheed(شهيد).

294
00:22:11,594 --> 00:22:14,295
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه told him;

295
00:22:15,805 --> 00:22:20,474
You mentioned that I'm a companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ and that he is pleased with me

296
00:22:20,986 --> 00:22:27,237
that is a blessing from Allah, and I cannot be credited for it, it is something that Allah gave me

297
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:32,065
and the concern that you see in my face,

298
00:22:32,427 --> 00:22:37,125
is because of my concern about you and your people.

299
00:22:38,181 --> 00:22:40,794
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying, the reason why you see me concerned

300
00:22:41,392 --> 00:22:43,394
 I'm thinking about you and your people,

301
00:22:43,569 --> 00:22:45,973
I'm thinking about the fate of the Muslims after me

302
00:22:46,112 --> 00:22:48,763
I'm thinking about this Khilafah(خِلَافَه) that's why, I'm concerned

303
00:22:49,855 --> 00:22:55,533
 it's not fear of death, it is because I'm concerned with the situation of my Ummah(امة)

304
00:22:59,072 --> 00:22:59,713
and then he said;

305
00:22:59,737 --> 00:23:07,662
واللهِ لَوْ أنًّ لِيْ طِلَاعُ الّأَرْضِ ذَهَبَ لَفْتَدَيْتُ بِه مِنْ عَذَابِ الله عَزُّوْأجَل قَبْلَ ألنّهَارًا

306
00:23:08,649 --> 00:23:13,493
 In the name of Allah if I had the whole world full of gold

307
00:23:14,944 --> 00:23:19,366
I would pay it to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْto ransom me from His punishment, before I see it.

308
00:23:20,676 --> 00:23:28,197
 when you read statements like this it puts you in shame.

309
00:23:29,068 --> 00:23:32,245
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) who's one of the 10 giving the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

310
00:23:32,617 --> 00:23:38,088
who has been given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة) on many occasions by Rasool Allah ﷺ

311
00:23:38,771 --> 00:23:43,223
Umar(عُمَر) who was The Statesman, who brought Islam to the world,

312
00:23:43,711 --> 00:23:46,956
Umar(عُمَر) one of the greatest Khulafah(خلفاء) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

313
00:23:47,529 --> 00:23:51,968
 Umar(عُمَر) who spread the Islam to the hearts of, thousands and thousands

314
00:23:51,993 --> 00:23:54,795
actually millions of people around the world.

315
00:23:55,131 --> 00:23:57,982
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he heard this Sahabah(صحابه), saying

316
00:23:58,364 --> 00:24:02,262
that you should rejoice with Jannah(جنة), you are the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ

317
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:04,661
you were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

318
00:24:04,783 --> 00:24:07,505
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I wish I can get out of it even

319
00:24:08,486 --> 00:24:10,364
with nothing for me and nothing against me.

320
00:24:11,055 --> 00:24:14,407
وَدَدْتُ لًوْ أَنِّيْ أخْرُجْ مِنْهَا كَفَّافْ لَا لِيْ وَلَا عَلِيْهََ

321
00:24:15,302 --> 00:24:18,558
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is desiring that all of his deeds are taken away

322
00:24:18,583 --> 00:24:19,944
and he makes it neutral, he breaks

323
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:24,803
Yani(يعني) Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) after all of these good deeds and he was still worried

324
00:24:25,252 --> 00:24:26,905
he's still feared Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

325
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:31,563
Therefore, those of us who do something good

326
00:24:31,588 --> 00:24:34,005
then they say: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله), I am a very good Muslim

327
00:24:34,029 --> 00:24:37,020
I'm practicing Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله), I've been praying for these many years

328
00:24:37,282 --> 00:24:42,780
I fasted, I did Hajj(حَجْ), I'm paying zakat, you know, I'm doing everything

329
00:24:44,152 --> 00:24:46,987
and they're so confident about it and they think that,

330
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,466
they have the keys of Jannah(جنة) in their pockets.

331
00:24:50,361 --> 00:24:55,583
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه after a long life of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

332
00:24:55,607 --> 00:24:59,642
and worshipping Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, on his death bed was worried that, he's not gonna make it.

333
00:25:03,715 --> 00:25:09,650
You know for us, for us now today, if you make zikr(زكر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

334
00:25:10,176 --> 00:25:12,785
you are so happy for the rest of the day, I've done zikr(زكر)

335
00:25:14,321 --> 00:25:16,436
I mean that's an achievement that's an act of worship

336
00:25:16,886 --> 00:25:19,669
for the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, zikr(زكر) was actually their rest.

337
00:25:20,936 --> 00:25:25,125
When they're making zikr(زكر), they're actually resting, from other works that they would do like

338
00:25:25,465 --> 00:25:27,402
fighting the enemy of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

339
00:25:27,719 --> 00:25:34,701
 so for them, zikr(زكر) was rest for the body and it was soothing for their hearts.

340
00:25:41,091 --> 00:25:42,872
Their entertainment was Qiyaam Ul-Lail(قيام اليل).

341
00:25:44,299 --> 00:25:47,892
Now, people would entertain themselves by going to nightclubs.

342
00:25:48,623 --> 00:25:53,278
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, would entertain, their hearts by standing and praying to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

343
00:25:53,612 --> 00:25:58,148
They would wait for those moments when they would be alone with Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

344
00:26:04,678 --> 00:26:07,734
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه passed away as Shaheed(شهيد)

345
00:26:08,757 --> 00:26:12,188
to fulfill the promise of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

346
00:26:14,591 --> 00:26:20,696
Rasool Allah صلواةالله وسلام عليه, along with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر) and Uthman(عثمان).

347
00:26:21,777 --> 00:26:25,234
Were standing on the mountain of Uhud(أحَد) and the mountain shook

348
00:26:28,434 --> 00:26:29,388
an earthquake.

349
00:26:30,196 --> 00:26:32,813
Rasool Allah ﷺ placed his hand on the mountain and said;

350
00:26:32,854 --> 00:26:37,791
أثْبُتْ أحُدْ فَإنمَاعَلَيْكَ نَبِيٌّ وَالصِدِيّقٌ وَ الشَهِيْدَيْنََ,

351
00:26:38,884 --> 00:26:43,469
Mountain of Uhud(أحَد) stay firm because on top of you, is a Prophet

352
00:26:43,828 --> 00:26:46,211
a Siddique(ألصديق) and two Shuhadah(شهداء),

353
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:49,425
Umar(عُمَر) and Uthman(عثمان)

354
00:26:52,692 --> 00:26:58,917
He died as a Shaheed(شهيد), as one of the greatest Shuhadah(شهداء) of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammad صلواةالله وسلام عليه

355
00:26:59,971 --> 00:27:05,358
because Shahadah(شهادة) is an honor and it's a choosing, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ chooses Shuhadah(شهداء)

356
00:27:05,511 --> 00:27:06,989
وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَآء

357
00:27:07,524 --> 00:27:10,270
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ loved Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) so much.

358
00:27:10,571 --> 00:27:13,507
He sent Shahadah(شهادة) to his door steps in Madina.

359
00:27:14,505 --> 00:27:16,809
We talked about the Dua(دُعَا) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he used to say

360
00:27:16,864 --> 00:27:21,339
اللهم إني أسئلك قَتْلًا في سبيلك وَ مَوةً فِيْ بَلَدِ نَبِيَّكََ

361
00:27:21,445 --> 00:27:27,398
O, Allah I asked you to be killed as a Shaheed(شهيد) and to die in the town of your Prophet

362
00:27:27,453 --> 00:27:32,076
 because there is a virtue in dying in Madina and there's a virtue in Shahadah(شهادة)

363
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:35,017
 he wanted them both, and then he would ask himself, the question?

364
00:27:35,224 --> 00:27:37,610
وَأَنَّ لِيَّ شَهَادَةْ وَأَيْنَ فِى الْمَدِيْنَهْ

365
00:27:37,634 --> 00:27:39,359
And how can I get Shahadah(شهادة) when I'm in Madina

366
00:27:40,105 --> 00:27:43,813
because Madina was the heartland of Islam, no danger gets through to Madina

367
00:27:44,464 --> 00:27:47,074
 nobody was ever assassinated Madina, he was the first one.

368
00:27:49,351 --> 00:27:51,423
Ibn Qayyim(إبن قيم), when he talks about the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

369
00:27:51,447 --> 00:27:54,195
He said: The Battle of Uhud(أحَد) is a victory, it's not a loss

370
00:27:55,317 --> 00:27:57,728
Ibn Qayyim(إبن قيم) considered it to be a victory in his book on Seerah(سيرة)

371
00:27:58,240 --> 00:28:03,461
he has some Allah Ho-Alam(الله أعلم) how many pages, he just went on, and on, and on, and on

372
00:28:04,020 --> 00:28:06,527
talking about how Uhud(أحَد) is a victory.

373
00:28:07,070 --> 00:28:08,093
He said: Why?

374
00:28:08,317 --> 00:28:12,325
Because it's a gold mine of Daroos(دروس), of lessons.

375
00:28:13,352 --> 00:28:23,163
Yes, it was a loss but because Allah use that loss to teach us all of these lessons, it's a victory.

376
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:28,506
Because the Ayaat(آيات) of Surah Al-Imran(سورة إلعمران) are commentating on what happened in Uhud(أحَد)

377
00:28:29,211 --> 00:28:32,176
he mentions one of these lessons, the Ayah(آية) that was revealed

378
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,798
ويتخذ منكم شهداء

379
00:28:34,224 --> 00:28:36,336
Allah is going to choose from among you Shuhadaa(شهداء)

380
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:38,822
it's just choice of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, it's not something, that you can get.

381
00:28:39,306 --> 00:28:42,714
It's something that Allah honors you by giving it to you.

382
00:28:44,168 --> 00:28:46,936
 And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, honored Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and gave it to him.

383
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:54,842
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was standing next to Umar(عُمَر), when he was dead,

384
00:28:55,857 --> 00:28:59,399
and when we say dead, we don't really mean that he is dead because

385
00:28:59,423 --> 00:29:02,505
وَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي  سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَات

386
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:04,304
He is not dead,  he's alive

387
00:29:04,652 --> 00:29:06,483
بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ۝

388
00:29:07,883 --> 00:29:11,803
They are given Rizq(رزق) by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and they are insides of green birds

389
00:29:12,039 --> 00:29:14,068
flying in paradise wherever they want.

390
00:29:14,676 --> 00:29:18,554
They just give the commands to the bird they are the pilots of those birds,

391
00:29:18,721 --> 00:29:21,161
 they fly with them, wherever they want.

392
00:29:21,329 --> 00:29:24,496
What kind of better simulation game can you get, and it's not a simulation

393
00:29:25,091 --> 00:29:29,455
it's a real thing you're driving that bird you're the pilot and it's flying,

394
00:29:29,816 --> 00:29:31,092
wherever you want in Jannah(جنة).

395
00:29:32,096 --> 00:29:36,246
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: I was standing next to Umar(عُمَر),

396
00:29:36,739 --> 00:29:41,081
when I felt the hand on my shoulders and I looked at it was Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

397
00:29:41,786 --> 00:29:45,188
 and Ali(علي) spoke the following words, he said;

398
00:29:45,821 --> 00:29:53,464
ما خلَّفْتُ أحَدًا، أحِبُّ أنْ ألّقَى الله بِمِثْلِيْ أمَلِيْهِ مِنْكََ

399
00:29:59,129 --> 00:30:07,146
There is nobody living today, whom I would rather meet Allah with his deeds rather than mine, than you.

400
00:30:09,023 --> 00:30:13,204
He said: I would rather meet Allah with your Amal(عمل) than mine.

401
00:30:14,141 --> 00:30:17,005
This is Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنهsaying that about Umar(عُمَر)

402
00:30:17,645 --> 00:30:20,119
 Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبد المطلب) was a neighbor of Umar(عُمَر), he said;

403
00:30:20,143 --> 00:30:24,745
I've never seen somebody like him, in his Ibadah(عبادة), night and day

404
00:30:25,366 --> 00:30:26,835
never waste a moment of his life.

405
00:30:30,436 --> 00:30:41,057
The Death of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), we cannot underestimate the effect it had on the Muslims of the day.

406
00:30:41,457 --> 00:30:43,512
 Ibn Abbasرضي الله عنه said;

407
00:30:44,258 --> 00:30:50,194
That whenever, I would pass next to a gathering, they would be crying, everyone was crying.

408
00:30:52,199 --> 00:30:57,665
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalibرضي الله عنه told the people because the people stopped eating

409
00:30:58,974 --> 00:31:02,177
they lost their appetite, they couldn't eat they were not drinking.

410
00:31:02,724 --> 00:31:03,494
Al-Abbas(العباس) said;

411
00:31:03,518 --> 00:31:09,251
يَا أيُّهَا النَّاسََ إنَّا رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قَدْ مَاتَ  فَأكَلْنَا بَعْدَ ه’ أشْرِبْنَا

412
00:31:09,535 --> 00:31:12,165
وَمَاتَ أبو بكر فَأكَلْنَا بَعْدَ ه’ أشْرِبْنَا

413
00:31:12,242 --> 00:31:16,595
لا بُدَّ لِنَّاسِ مِنْ أكلِنْ، وَ شُرْبٍ مَدَّ يَدَّه’ ثُمَ أكَّلََ

414
00:31:17,243 --> 00:31:20,780
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: O people when Rasool Allah ﷺ died, we ate,

415
00:31:21,323 --> 00:31:25,731
when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) died we ate and we cannot survive today without eating.

416
00:31:30,532 --> 00:31:34,627
 Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), he was weeping and then he said;

417
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:39,555
إنَّا عمر كَانَ حَسْنَنْ لِلّإسلامِ يَدْخُلُوْنَ فِيْهِ وَلَا يَخْرُجُوْنَ

418
00:31:40,538 --> 00:31:45,450
فَلَمَّا مَاتَ إنْ سَلَمَ ذَلِكَ حَسْن فَالنَّاسُ يَخْرُوْجُوْنَ مِنَ الّاِسْلَامَ

419
00:31:46,611 --> 00:31:48,668
Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه said:

420
00:31:49,549 --> 00:31:52,149
Umar(عُمَر) was the fortress of a Islam

421
00:31:52,476 --> 00:31:54,942
when people come into it, they do not leave

422
00:31:55,601 --> 00:31:59,701
 and when he died that fortress fell down.

423
00:31:59,912 --> 00:32:02,112
So, now people are walking out of Islam.

424
00:32:03,616 --> 00:32:07,823
you know it's amazing how one man could do so much for the religion

425
00:32:07,847 --> 00:32:12,307
I mean, even though we don't take it as a standard but it's something that could be mentioned

426
00:32:13,112 --> 00:32:15,636
from a secular point of view not from a religious point of view.

427
00:32:15,677 --> 00:32:17,151
From a secular point of view.

428
00:32:18,534 --> 00:32:23,005
When Michael Hart studied the lives of the great,

429
00:32:24,624 --> 00:32:32,211
the only two Muslims that he chose were Rasool Allah ﷺ and he was number one obviously

430
00:32:32,606 --> 00:32:35,383
and by the way he had to apologize for that in the introduction to his book.

431
00:32:36,035 --> 00:32:36,321
He said;

432
00:32:36,368 --> 00:32:38,297
Some of my readers might not like

433
00:32:38,733 --> 00:32:44,566
the fact that I have chosen Muhammadﷺ to head the list, of my greatest man that ever lived

434
00:32:44,986 --> 00:32:52,256
but he was the only man who was supremely successful on both the secular and religious fronts.

435
00:32:52,930 --> 00:32:53,700
 And then he said;

436
00:32:53,906 --> 00:33:00,821
If I would just take Muhammadﷺ the military leader that in itself would qualify him to make it on the list,

437
00:33:01,550 --> 00:33:05,362
not looking at the Prophet, the teacher, the family man

438
00:33:06,096 --> 00:33:09,457
just Muhammadﷺ the military leader alone would qualify him.

439
00:33:09,702 --> 00:33:12,528
He's looking at it obviously from a secular point of view.

440
00:33:13,192 --> 00:33:21,692
Otherwise, the lowest of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ is greater than the greatest Kaffir(كافر) on his list.

441
00:33:21,799 --> 00:33:26,372
But the thing is and he is looking at it from a secular point of view and he said;

442
00:33:26,751 --> 00:33:34,959
My standard was, how wide the influence was and for how long did it last.

443
00:33:37,408 --> 00:33:44,810
The only other Muslim who made it to his list was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

444
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:50,787
 because of his achievements as the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims

445
00:33:52,929 --> 00:33:56,777
within 10 years, how wide Islam has spread.

446
00:34:00,742 --> 00:34:06,714
Abu Obaidah رضي الله عنه before Umar(عُمَر) would die, He would say

447
00:34:07,090 --> 00:34:09,368
إنْ مَّاتَ عمر  رَقَّلْ إسْلام

448
00:34:10,294 --> 00:34:13,786
If Umar(عُمَر) would die, Islam would become weaker.

449
00:34:14,886 --> 00:34:18,027
So, the people would ask him why do you say that?

450
00:34:19,875 --> 00:34:21,126
Islam is not in need of Umar(عُمَر)

451
00:34:21,151 --> 00:34:24,222
why would it become weaker, he would say;

452
00:34:27,028 --> 00:34:31,920
قَالَ سَتَرَوْنَ مَا أقُوْلُوْ إنْ بًقِيْتُمْْ

453
00:34:32,432 --> 00:34:37,260
You will see that what I'm saying is true, if you live after he dies

454
00:34:38,254 --> 00:34:44,601
وَ أمَّا هُوَ فَإن وُلِيَ وَالٍى بَعْدَه’ فأخَذَ هُمْ بِمَا كَانَ عمر يَاخُذْهُمْ

455
00:34:44,838 --> 00:34:50,438
لَمْ يُطِعْ لَه’ النَّاسََ وَلَمْ  يَحْمِلُه’ وَ إنْ ضَعُفَ عَنْهُم قَتَلُُ

456
00:34:50,916 --> 00:34:58,686
He said: Because if the Khalifah(خليفه) after Umar(عُمَر) tries to apply the same strictness and rules of Umar(عُمَر),

457
00:34:59,321 --> 00:35:01,017
 people will not accept it, from him.

458
00:35:02,748 --> 00:35:06,305
And if that Khalifah(خليفه) is weak then they would kill him.

459
00:35:08,555 --> 00:35:12,390
Only Umar(عُمَر) could command the people in that firmness

460
00:35:13,125 --> 00:35:18,170
because his personality was suitable for it, if somebody else tries to do it, the people wouldn't buy it

461
00:35:19,265 --> 00:35:20,622
 and then Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) said;

462
00:35:21,179 --> 00:35:28,187
ما اُحِبُّ أنَّ لِيْ مَا تَطلُوْعُ عليهِ الشَّمْسََ وَتَغْرُبْ وَاَنْ أبْقَا بَعْدَ عمر، يَوْمً وَاحِدًَ

463
00:35:29,904 --> 00:35:34,721
Even if I would get everything the sun rises on

464
00:35:36,538 --> 00:35:37,552
 meaning the whole earth

465
00:35:37,632 --> 00:35:43,771
if you would give me the whole earth and ask me to live for a day after Umar(عُمَر), I would refuse

466
00:35:46,238 --> 00:35:48,296
He wouldn't want to live after Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

467
00:35:54,685 --> 00:35:56,993
How old was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he passed away?

468
00:35:58,944 --> 00:36:01,884
Muawiya Bin Abi Sufiyan(معاويه بن أبي سفيان) says;

469
00:36:04,051 --> 00:36:08,851
تُوُفِيَّ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، وَهُوَ إبْنُ الثَّلَاثٍ وَسِتِّيْنَ

470
00:36:09,581 --> 00:36:13,806
تُوُفِيَّ أبوبكر، وَهُوَ إبْنُ الثَّلَاثٍ وَسِتِّيْنَ،

471
00:36:14,300 --> 00:36:19,168
 تُوُفِيَّ عمر، وَهُوَ إبْنُ الثَّلَاثٍ وَسِتِّيْنَ، رواه مسلم

472
00:36:19,705 --> 00:36:22,615
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away and he was 63 years old,

473
00:36:23,471 --> 00:36:26,452
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) passed away and he was 63 years old,

474
00:36:26,808 --> 00:36:30,128
and Umar(عُمَر) passed away and he was 63 years old.

475
00:36:32,264 --> 00:36:35,025
They were together in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and they died at the same age

476
00:36:35,183 --> 00:36:37,483
and they will be brought together on the Day of Judgment.

477
00:36:37,682 --> 00:36:39,317
They were the closest friends.

478
00:36:40,881 --> 00:36:45,871
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said I would remember Rasool Allah ﷺ saying;

479
00:36:46,337 --> 00:36:47,942
I left with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر)

480
00:36:48,308 --> 00:36:49,899
I came with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر),

481
00:36:50,209 --> 00:36:51,759
I went with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر).

482
00:36:52,723 --> 00:36:57,071
Always Rasool Allah ﷺ would mention his name along with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

483
00:37:02,472 --> 00:37:07,270
He was buried by Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه Sohaib(صهيب) and Saeed Bin Zayd(سعيد بن زيد),

484
00:37:07,653 --> 00:37:11,638
these are the three who lowered him in his grave.

485
00:37:13,121 --> 00:37:14,924
Before Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) passed away

486
00:37:16,822 --> 00:37:19,804
he told his son Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر), he said;

487
00:37:20,677 --> 00:37:22,777
Go to Umm Momineen(أم المؤمنين), Ayesha(عائشه)

488
00:37:24,854 --> 00:37:29,515
and tell her that Umar(عُمَر), and do not say Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)

489
00:37:29,539 --> 00:37:32,055
because I'm no, Ameer(أمير) of the Momineen(مؤمنين) anymore,

490
00:37:33,696 --> 00:37:41,329
say Umar(عُمَر) is asking for your permission to allow him to be buried with his two companions

491
00:37:42,932 --> 00:37:44,669
 that room belongs Ayesha(عائشه).

492
00:37:45,058 --> 00:37:51,132
So, it was her property, so he needs to get her permission to be buried in there

493
00:37:51,827 --> 00:37:54,605
and he didn't want it to come as an order from order from Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين),

494
00:37:54,663 --> 00:37:56,059
he said: Tell her that its Umar(عُمَر)

495
00:37:56,278 --> 00:37:58,511
because Umar(عُمَر) is not the Ameer(أمير) of the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) anymore.

496
00:37:59,999 --> 00:38:05,817
Tell her that Umar(عُمَر) wants to be buried with his friends and come back to me,

497
00:38:07,305 --> 00:38:10,623
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر), he said: I went and I found her crying

498
00:38:12,346 --> 00:38:16,554
and I told her, Umar(عُمَر) is giving you his Salam(سلام),

499
00:38:17,867 --> 00:38:21,693
and he is seeking your permission to be buried with his two companions.

500
00:38:22,881 --> 00:38:27,139
Ayesha رضي الله عنهsaid: I wanted that place for myself.

501
00:38:28,261 --> 00:38:32,679
However, today I'm going to give Umar(عُمَر) favor over myself.

502
00:38:35,232 --> 00:38:38,162
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) went back, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

503
00:38:38,186 --> 00:38:42,680
When he saw Abdullah(عبدالله) coming, he said: Have me sit upright,

504
00:38:43,419 --> 00:38:44,656
he was so concerned about it.

505
00:38:45,299 --> 00:38:47,831
And then he told Abdullah(عبدالله), What news do you have?

506
00:38:48,256 --> 00:38:50,338
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: The news that you like,

507
00:38:51,134 --> 00:38:55,593
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: There was nothing more concerning to me than that.

508
00:38:57,379 --> 00:39:00,105
But then he said: When I die, go to her again.

509
00:39:00,130 --> 00:39:03,843
Because he didn't want her to take a decision that she might regret.

510
00:39:03,867 --> 00:39:06,835
He said: When I die, go to her again

511
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:11,450
and tell her that Umar(عُمَر) is seeking permission to be buried with his friends.

512
00:39:11,955 --> 00:39:14,364
If she allows me in than Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله),

513
00:39:14,677 --> 00:39:17,842
if she doesn't take me and burry me with the Muslims.

514
00:39:20,161 --> 00:39:26,336
So, they were carrying the body of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and they brought him in, to the room of Ayesha(عائشه),

515
00:39:26,884 --> 00:39:28,022
 and they knocked the door and they said;

516
00:39:28,062 --> 00:39:31,279
 Umar(عُمَر) is asking for your permission to come in.

517
00:39:31,678 --> 00:39:32,858
She said; He's welcome.

518
00:39:34,650 --> 00:39:38,134
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Ayesha رضي الله عنه, after Umar(عُمَر) was buried, she said;

519
00:39:40,439 --> 00:39:46,144
Whenever, I would come into my room, I would have my clothes wrapped all over me.

520
00:39:47,563 --> 00:39:50,722
I was so shy from Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

521
00:39:50,747 --> 00:39:52,185
even though, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) he is buried

522
00:39:54,564 --> 00:39:57,013
but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) his personality had so much respect.

523
00:39:57,045 --> 00:39:58,314
Even when he was in the grave.

524
00:39:58,857 --> 00:40:02,067
She said: I had to have my hijab(حجاب) on, when I come into my room.

525
00:40:07,938 --> 00:40:10,476
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Ayesha(عائشه), she said;

526
00:40:10,894 --> 00:40:14,790
مَرَّاعَ إبنِ الخَّطاب عَلِمَ أنَّه’ خُلِقَ غِنَّى إلِّاالّإسلام

527
00:40:15,423 --> 00:40:20,761
Whoever, sees Umar(عُمَر), realizes that he was created to give strength to Islam.

528
00:40:22,190 --> 00:40:26,951
Allah created him, Allah made him, to give victory to this religion.

529
00:40:28,442 --> 00:40:33,296
You know, everything is Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ things don't just happen haphazardly.

530
00:40:34,507 --> 00:40:38,504
It was part of the plan of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that was ordained

531
00:40:38,995 --> 00:40:41,409
that Umar(عُمَر) would be created for that purpose.

532
00:40:41,770 --> 00:40:45,708
The propagator of this religion, the establisher of its institutions,

533
00:40:46,199 --> 00:40:50,301
the Khalifah(خليفه), who would establish the rule of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on land

534
00:40:51,968 --> 00:40:53,408
and then she said;

535
00:40:53,619 --> 00:40:55,032
كَانَ وَالله أحْوَزِيْعً

536
00:40:55,435 --> 00:40:57,523
He was a very disciplined and strict man.

537
00:40:58,324 --> 00:40:59,376
نَسِيْجٌ وَاحْدةَ

538
00:40:59,732 --> 00:41:01,644
He was made from a different fabric.

539
00:41:03,601 --> 00:41:05,853
قَدْ أعَدَّ لِلْأمُوْرِ أقْرَانُهَا

540
00:41:06,514 --> 00:41:12,004
He has prepared for every affair, the appropriate response.

541
00:41:12,438 --> 00:41:15,641
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was so competent, strong, confident

542
00:41:16,090 --> 00:41:19,658
that any situation that arises he would be able to handle it,

543
00:41:21,632 --> 00:41:25,985
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) would say about Umar(عُمَر) these are authentic narrations.

544
00:41:26,325 --> 00:41:29,626
لَوْ أنَّ عِلْمَ عمر وُضِعَ فِيْ كَفَّتِ الّمِيْزَانَ

545
00:41:29,888 --> 00:41:33,944
وَوُضِعَ عِلْمُ الّأرضِ فِيْ كَفَّ لَرَجَهَا عِلْم عمر

546
00:41:35,307 --> 00:41:38,346
If the knowledge of Umar(عُمَر) is placed on one side of the scale

547
00:41:38,717 --> 00:41:42,589
and the knowledge of the whole earth is placed on the other side of the scale,

548
00:41:44,742 --> 00:41:46,906
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)'s knowledge would be heavier.

549
00:41:48,664 --> 00:41:51,957
His knowledge is heavier than the knowledge of everyone else, he would say;

550
00:41:52,812 --> 00:41:57,149
إِنِّيْ لَأحْسِبُ أَنَّ عمرذَهَبَبِ تِسْعَتِ أَعْشَارِ الْعِلم

551
00:41:57,613 --> 00:42:04,386
I believe that Umar(عُمَر) has left and he has taken away with him 9 tenth of all knowledge,

552
00:42:06,116 --> 00:42:11,042
nine tenths of the knowledge of the earth departed with the departure of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

553
00:42:15,034 --> 00:42:15,567
 He would say;

554
00:42:15,592 --> 00:42:21,106
كَانَ إِسْلَامَ عمرفَتْحً، وَهِجْرَتُه’نَصْرًا، وَإِمَارَته’ رَحْمةَ

555
00:42:22,161 --> 00:42:24,125
The Islam of Umar(عُمَر) was an opening,

556
00:42:25,178 --> 00:42:26,932
his Hijrah(هجرة) was victory,

557
00:42:27,702 --> 00:42:30,352
and his reign was mercy.

558
00:42:31,776 --> 00:42:34,303
 Abu Talha Al-Ansariرضي الله عنهwould say;

559
00:42:34,726 --> 00:42:37,372
والله مَا مِنْ أهْلِ بَيْتٍ مِنَّ الّمُسْلِمِيْنَ

560
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:42,376
إلَا وَقَدْ دَخَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ فِيْ مَوْتِ عمر نَقْصٌ فِي دِيْنِهِمْ وَدُنْيَاهُمْ

561
00:42:43,325 --> 00:42:47,000
In the name of Allah, every single Muslim house,

562
00:42:48,718 --> 00:42:54,698
is deficient in its religion and its Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), because of the death of Umar رضي الله عنه.

563
00:42:55,765 --> 00:42:58,680
The death of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) has caused a deficiency,

564
00:42:59,014 --> 00:43:01,806
in the dean and Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) of every Muslim household.

565
00:43:05,521 --> 00:43:09,462
Hudaifa رضي الله عنه Bin Yaman(بن يمان) would say and this is Sahih(صحيح) narration;

566
00:43:09,904 --> 00:43:13,055
إنَّما كان مَثَلُ الَإسلامِ  أيَّامَ عمر

567
00:43:13,748 --> 00:43:19,372
مِثْلِى مُقْبِلٍ لَمْ يَزَلْ فِي إقبَالٍ فَلَمَّا قُتِلَ أدْبَرْ فَلَمْ يَزَلْ فِي إدْبَارْ

568
00:43:20,384 --> 00:43:24,042
When Umar(عُمَر) was alive, Islam was approaching and was drawing near.

569
00:43:24,382 --> 00:43:28,040
And when Umar(عُمَر) died, it turned around and was drawing further away.

570
00:43:29,754 --> 00:43:40,060
Muawiyah Bin Abi Sufiyan(معاويه ابن ابي سفيان) would say about the first two Khulafaa(خلفاء);

571
00:43:40,775 --> 00:43:46,636
أمَّا أبو بكر فَلَمْ يُرِدِدُّنِيَا وَلَم تُرِدْه،

572
00:43:47,413 --> 00:43:51,113
وأمَّا عمر فَلَمْ يُرِدِدُّنِيَا فَأرَدَتْه،

573
00:43:51,708 --> 00:43:55,464
وَأمَّا نَحْنُ فَتَمَرَّغْنَا فِيْهَا ظَهْرَلِّبَتْنَ

574
00:43:56,704 --> 00:43:58,630
Muawiya(معاويه) when he was Khalifah(خليفه) he would say;

575
00:43:59,309 --> 00:44:04,614
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did not want this world and this world and not want him,

576
00:44:06,180 --> 00:44:10,386
Umar(عُمَر) did not want this world, but this world was chasing after him.

577
00:44:11,689 --> 00:44:16,965
But us, we have sunk ourselves in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) from front to back.

578
00:44:17,975 --> 00:44:20,926
We have got ourselves buried in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

579
00:44:26,501 --> 00:44:30,002
Ali Bin Abdullah Bin Abbas(علي بن عبدالله بن عباس) the son of Abdullah Bin Abbas(عبدالله بن عباس),

580
00:44:30,764 --> 00:44:32,922
he visited the Khalifah(خليفه), Abdul Malik Bin Marwan(عبدالملك بن مروان).

581
00:44:33,593 --> 00:44:36,440
It was a very cold day in Ash-Sham(ألشام), in Syria

582
00:44:36,925 --> 00:44:46,585
and he was in a tent covered with some very fancy fabrics

583
00:44:47,394 --> 00:44:52,838
and he had four heaters with him in the tent, four furnaces very comfortable.

584
00:44:54,089 --> 00:44:57,808
So, Ali(علي) came in and he was shivering because it's very cold.

585
00:44:59,164 --> 00:45:02,481
So, Abdul Malik(عبدالملك) said: It seems to be a cold day.

586
00:45:03,266 --> 00:45:07,247
Ali(علي) said: It is the coldest day that people of Ash-Sham(ألشام) have experienced.

587
00:45:10,314 --> 00:45:14,925
And then Abdul Malik Bin Marwan(عبدالملك بن مروان), started talking about Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

588
00:45:16,188 --> 00:45:24,951
and he was criticizing the attachment of people to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and speaking against it.

589
00:45:27,361 --> 00:45:32,678
And then he said: And here is Muawiya(معاويه), for 40 years.

590
00:45:33,423 --> 00:45:36,093
For the first 20 years, he was the Ameer(امير) of Ash-Sham(ألشام).

591
00:45:36,118 --> 00:45:38,527
And for the last 20 years, he was the Khalifah(خليفه),

592
00:45:39,241 --> 00:45:41,101
and what good did Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) do for him.

593
00:45:41,596 --> 00:45:43,372
May Allah have mercy on Umar(عُمَر).

594
00:45:43,696 --> 00:45:46,590
He was the most knowledgeable among us, when it came to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

595
00:45:47,622 --> 00:45:50,528
He is the man, who knew what Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was about.

596
00:45:51,737 --> 00:45:55,844
He lived a very disciplined life, a life of austerity.

597
00:45:56,121 --> 00:45:58,863
And he died without being scratched by Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

598
00:46:00,312 --> 00:46:02,308
Muawiya(معاويه) said that Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was pursuing him,

599
00:46:03,109 --> 00:46:04,752
Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was running after him,

600
00:46:06,078 --> 00:46:09,381
but he did not want Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and he saved himself from it.

601
00:46:13,898 --> 00:46:15,274
الحمد لله رب العلمين

602
00:46:15,298 --> 00:46:23,949
Who allowed us to come together and talk about the Seerah(سيرة) of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

603
00:46:25,385 --> 00:46:37,376
It's a blessing of Allah on us, to live with Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه for these 18 evenings.

604
00:46:39,185 --> 00:46:42,777
We asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to make us of those who would listen to the words

605
00:46:42,871 --> 00:46:46,923
and follow the best of them. Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

606
00:46:46,955 --> 00:46:48,787
لَقَدْ كَانَ فِي قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ

607
00:46:49,587 --> 00:46:51,850
There are lessons in their stories,

608
00:46:52,558 --> 00:46:59,243
Brothers and sisters, the objective of the stories is not entertainment.

609
00:47:00,864 --> 00:47:02,940
The objective is to take heed,

610
00:47:03,741 --> 00:47:04,670
 and to benefit,

611
00:47:05,138 --> 00:47:06,035
and to learn,

612
00:47:07,328 --> 00:47:09,471
 and then to apply what you learn.

613
00:47:12,265 --> 00:47:18,894
I'm sure that now, you have more love of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

614
00:47:18,926 --> 00:47:21,701
because that is how, it is with the Saleheen(صالحين).

615
00:47:23,314 --> 00:47:26,166
With the Saleheen(صالحين) the more you know about them, the more you love them,

616
00:47:27,037 --> 00:47:31,049
with the Fasiqeen(فاسقين) the more you know about them, the more you despise them.

617
00:47:34,154 --> 00:47:35,771
The more you study about Rasool Allah ﷺ,

618
00:47:35,835 --> 00:47:37,270
 the more you study about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

619
00:47:37,294 --> 00:47:38,533
the more you study about the Sahabah(صحابه)

620
00:47:38,573 --> 00:47:40,041
 the more impressed you become.

621
00:47:44,191 --> 00:47:46,775
But we have to take that into action,

622
00:47:47,999 --> 00:47:50,068
now that we know about Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

623
00:47:50,092 --> 00:47:53,427
if we don't do anything about that knowledge and we sit, on it.

624
00:47:53,791 --> 00:47:57,998
We will be held accountable on the Day of Judgment for knowing that and then doing nothing about it.

625
00:47:58,422 --> 00:48:01,833
Sometimes, it's better to be ignorant then to know

626
00:48:02,418 --> 00:48:05,014
because if you know and you don't do anything you're worst,

627
00:48:05,831 --> 00:48:09,135
you're in a worst situation than somebody who's Jahil(جاهل),

628
00:48:09,842 --> 00:48:12,503
because the ignorant can be excused on the Day of Judgment,

629
00:48:12,988 --> 00:48:14,361
but the knowledgeable cannot.

630
00:48:15,821 --> 00:48:21,452
So, we want to take the life of Umar(عُمَر) into implementation.

631
00:48:22,262 --> 00:48:25,756
Now, the reason why we're talking about the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم is

632
00:48:25,781 --> 00:48:28,639
Because their way, was the best way,

633
00:48:29,913 --> 00:48:33,312
there are many righteous Muslims in every generation in every century

634
00:48:33,336 --> 00:48:35,045
there are good Muslims,

635
00:48:35,989 --> 00:48:40,306
but none of them comes close to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

636
00:48:41,282 --> 00:48:43,420
We could have chose to talk about the great scholar,

637
00:48:44,771 --> 00:48:46,752
we could chose to talk about the great Mujahid(مجاهد),

638
00:48:47,834 --> 00:48:50,099
we could chose to talk about a great Daiyah(داعيه)

639
00:48:51,259 --> 00:48:56,443
but none of them would come close to the personalities of the Sahabah(صحابه) like Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه,

640
00:48:57,293 --> 00:48:59,117
the Sahabah(صحابه) represent the middle way,

641
00:48:59,466 --> 00:49:01,196
they represent the perfect way,

642
00:49:01,749 --> 00:49:07,585
there is something, of everything that you would find in their lives, that could benefit you,

643
00:49:08,222 --> 00:49:12,346
in your family, in your work, in your Da'wah(دعوة).

644
00:49:12,585 --> 00:49:17,089
You would find the reference, for that in the life of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

645
00:49:18,335 --> 00:49:20,992
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم they represented the middle way.

646
00:49:21,715 --> 00:49:23,893
So, they were not only doing Da'wah(دعوة).

647
00:49:24,663 --> 00:49:26,533
 They were not only doing Jihad(جهاد)

648
00:49:26,739 --> 00:49:29,501
they were not only doing Ilm(علم), but they did them all.

649
00:49:31,419 --> 00:49:34,373
 And they gave the right proportion to the different Ibadaat(عبادات).

650
00:49:34,799 --> 00:49:36,594
 The problem today with us is,

651
00:49:36,888 --> 00:49:40,903
we're like the blind men who went to visit the elephant in the zoo.

652
00:49:41,696 --> 00:49:43,217
You must have heard of that parable.

653
00:49:43,739 --> 00:49:46,205
Three blind men wanted to go to the zoo,

654
00:49:46,928 --> 00:49:48,188
and experience the elephant.

655
00:49:48,684 --> 00:49:50,355
They've never seen an elephant in their life.

656
00:49:50,379 --> 00:49:52,359
They want to experience what an elephant is.

657
00:49:52,808 --> 00:49:54,141
So, they were taken to the zoo.

658
00:49:54,721 --> 00:49:57,750
One of them grabbed the ear of the elephant,

659
00:49:58,655 --> 00:50:01,330
the other one grabbed the foot

660
00:50:01,613 --> 00:50:03,941
and the third one grabbed the tail,

661
00:50:05,243 --> 00:50:08,650
when they went back home People ask them tell us about the elephant.

662
00:50:09,162 --> 00:50:11,845
So, the first one said: The elephant is very thin and broad.

663
00:50:13,240 --> 00:50:15,216
Second one said: No! that's not right.

664
00:50:15,843 --> 00:50:17,438
The elephant is like a pillar

665
00:50:18,571 --> 00:50:21,681
the third one said: No! No! No! Both of you are wrong.

666
00:50:22,102 --> 00:50:23,729
The elephant is like a rope.

667
00:50:25,669 --> 00:50:28,460
Now they were all right but they were all wrong.

668
00:50:29,816 --> 00:50:33,520
They're all right in describing their experience

669
00:50:34,270 --> 00:50:38,440
but they were wrong in thinking that their experience was the only right one.

670
00:50:40,346 --> 00:50:44,676
So sometimes we find brothers going in one direction, they're running in one direction

671
00:50:45,008 --> 00:50:48,780
 all what they want to do is learn knowledge and that's it and forget about anything else

672
00:50:49,019 --> 00:50:51,715
and seeking knowledge is the best thing under the sun

673
00:50:52,040 --> 00:50:57,746
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said, this about the students of Ilm(علم) and the angels ask Allah to forgive them.

674
00:50:58,760 --> 00:51:02,276
Somebody else will go into Zuhud(ذهد) and Ibadah(عبادة) Qayyam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل) Sayyam(صيام)

675
00:51:02,300 --> 00:51:05,667
and will narrate, all of the Hadith(حديث) about how great all of that is.

676
00:51:06,542 --> 00:51:11,259
Somebody, else will go into Da'wah(دعوة) and say it's very important to guide the people to Islam we need to do that

677
00:51:12,363 --> 00:51:16,008
 we will not have the right perspective, until we look at the lives of those Sahabah(صحابه)

678
00:51:16,033 --> 00:51:17,972
How did they spend their time?

679
00:51:18,591 --> 00:51:19,951
What did they do?

680
00:51:21,705 --> 00:51:25,726
What was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) busy with during his Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

681
00:51:26,770 --> 00:51:32,023
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, would worship during the night and would fast during the day.

682
00:51:32,754 --> 00:51:37,262
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه would go in his nightly patrols

683
00:51:37,621 --> 00:51:39,986
taking care of the needy, among the Muslims.

684
00:51:40,451 --> 00:51:43,617
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would spend his day financing

685
00:51:43,641 --> 00:51:46,918
and sending armies to fight Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

686
00:51:48,502 --> 00:51:51,243
That is how, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم spend their time

687
00:51:51,267 --> 00:51:56,531
and they are the they are the greatest generation of this Ummah(امة).

688
00:51:57,213 --> 00:52:01,553
So, we need to follow their way, because their way is the best way.

689
00:52:02,474 --> 00:52:09,155
So let's all learn from the life of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and apply it in our ourselves.

690
00:52:09,870 --> 00:52:13,058
We asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْto accept from us

691
00:52:13,264 --> 00:52:16,542
this deed of coming together and studying about Umar(عُمَر)

692
00:52:17,305 --> 00:52:23,475
we ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to make us of those who listen to the words and follow the best of them.

693
00:52:23,956 --> 00:52:28,860
We asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to make us of those, who would not only spread the word about Umar(عُمَر)

694
00:52:29,187 --> 00:52:31,326
 but would live the life of Umar(عُمَر) in themselves.

695
00:52:32,103 --> 00:52:39,235
we asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, finally to bring us together with them, in Jannah(جنة).

696
00:52:42,060 --> 00:52:45,396
I'm sure that you have a lot of questions, about the life of Umar(عُمَر)

697
00:52:47,162 --> 00:52:49,935
and you don't want to ask them because you know that I don't know the answer.

698
00:52:52,383 --> 00:52:57,009
Keep those questions In Sha Allah Ho Ta'ala(إن شاءالله تعالى) when you meet Umar(عُمَر) in Jannah(جنة).

699
00:52:57,636 --> 00:52:59,390
Ask him whatever, you want.

700
00:53:00,565 --> 00:53:03,766
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The people of Jannah(جنة) are

701
00:53:03,790 --> 00:53:05,111
عَلَى قَلْبِ الرَّجُلٌ وَاحِدْْ

702
00:53:06,388 --> 00:53:11,931
The people of Jannah(جنة) have their hearts are so much in love with each other

703
00:53:11,956 --> 00:53:13,725
as if it is the heart of one man.

704
00:53:15,018 --> 00:53:17,291
So, when you want to meet with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

705
00:53:17,826 --> 00:53:19,755
he will immediately, accept your request.

706
00:53:20,774 --> 00:53:23,633
And he will give you all the time in the world that you want.

707
00:53:23,657 --> 00:53:29,268
Because in Jannah(جنة), there are no deadlines, there's no limit, it's infinity

708
00:53:29,757 --> 00:53:32,139
it's not a million years, it's not a billion years.

709
00:53:32,424 --> 00:53:35,043
 It goes on, and on and on and on.

710
00:53:35,770 --> 00:53:42,496
You know the Energizer Bunny, it will run out of energy, before you die in Jannah(جنة)

711
00:53:42,852 --> 00:53:44,085
because you never will die.

712
00:53:45,404 --> 00:53:48,769
It never ends, so you can meet with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

713
00:53:48,918 --> 00:53:50,860
You can ask him about how he became Muslim.

714
00:53:51,356 --> 00:53:53,683
You can ask him about his Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

715
00:53:53,890 --> 00:53:57,447
you can ask him about his Da'wah(دعوة) you can ask him about his Ibadah(عبادة)

716
00:53:58,431 --> 00:54:02,313
He will give you a month, a year appointment as long as you want.

717
00:54:03,304 --> 00:54:05,144
He has all the time and you have all the time.

718
00:54:07,375 --> 00:54:09,881
إِخْوَانًا عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُتَقَابِلِينَ

719
00:54:10,292 --> 00:54:13,053
You will be brothers reclining on thrones.

720
00:54:16,106 --> 00:54:18,790
After knowing all of this about the Sahabah(صحابه)

721
00:54:18,903 --> 00:54:20,842
and after knowing this about Al-Jannah(جنة)

722
00:54:21,390 --> 00:54:25,669
only an insane person would turn down such an offer.

723
00:54:28,283 --> 00:54:32,771
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said: I don't know how somebody could know about Jannah(جنة) and then sleep

724
00:54:33,822 --> 00:54:37,842
and how can there be anybody who knows about An-Naar(النار) and then sleep

725
00:54:38,760 --> 00:54:43,112
but we are living in a state of sleep, unawareness.

726
00:54:43,937 --> 00:54:47,081
And the problem with many of us they only wake up when they die.

727
00:54:48,054 --> 00:54:52,223
We ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ us to wake us up, way before that and to grant us Tauba(التوبة)

728
00:54:52,704 --> 00:54:54,236
that will forgive all of our sins

729
00:54:54,863 --> 00:54:57,246
and to make us die as Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as a shaheed(شهيد)

730
00:54:58,250 --> 00:55:01,758
and to bring us, together with them in Jannat-Ul-Fidausi(الجنة الفردوسي).

731
00:55:02,497 --> 00:55:06,499
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ

732
00:55:08,557 --> 00:55:10,679
I have made many mistakes.

733
00:55:11,512 --> 00:55:14,569
Usually speakers would make the assumption if I made mistakes

734
00:55:14,838 --> 00:55:17,415
they are for myself, but I definitely did make mistakes.

735
00:55:18,255 --> 00:55:20,855
So, these mistakes are from myself.

736
00:55:21,442 --> 00:55:23,928
If there was any good it is from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

737
00:55:24,220 --> 00:55:26,011
We ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to forgive us all

738
00:55:26,398 --> 00:55:30,999
سُبْحَانَكَ الله هُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكْ نَشْهَدُ الله إِلَهَ إِلَّا أَنْت نَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَنَتُوْبُ عَلَيْكَ

739
00:55:31,608 --> 00:55:34,118
Some of the questions, what we have.

740
00:55:36,540 --> 00:55:40,224
Umar(عُمَر) told Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) to do Jihad(جهاد) at the time of Jumu'ah(جمعه).

741
00:55:40,302 --> 00:55:43,112
Does this mean that Jumu'ah(جمعه) is not compulsory on the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) also

742
00:55:43,131 --> 00:55:47,607
 what is the best time to make Dua(دُعَا) on the day of Jumu'ah(جمعه).

743
00:55:48,336 --> 00:55:50,753
Jumu'ah(جمعه) is not compulsory on anybody who's traveling.

744
00:55:51,356 --> 00:55:53,398
Anybody who's traveling and the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) are traveling,

745
00:55:54,117 --> 00:55:57,270
a traveler does have the choice of praying Jumu'ah(جمعه) or praying Zuhar(ظهر).

746
00:55:58,250 --> 00:56:01,684
And the time of Dua(دُعَا) on Jumu'ah(جمعه), some scholars say

747
00:56:01,765 --> 00:56:03,949
it is the time, when the Imam(اِمَام) is on the Mimber(ممبر),

748
00:56:04,305 --> 00:56:09,765
and some other scholars say it is the time right before Maghrib(مغرب) of the Day of Jumu'ah(جمعه),

749
00:56:10,453 --> 00:56:14,839
it's either of these two times, that is the time when the Dua(دُعَا) is accepted.

750
00:56:16,167 --> 00:56:18,901
There's a sister in our school who wears the full hijab(حجاب) and

751
00:56:18,926 --> 00:56:21,475
claims that Islam is not equal or fair to women.

752
00:56:22,026 --> 00:56:31,151
She tells the teachers that in Islam women are not allowed to marry four times, whereas men are.

753
00:56:31,681 --> 00:56:35,081
This goes back to a very serious problem,

754
00:56:35,370 --> 00:56:39,171
which is called Ash-Shubuhaat(ألشبهات), doubts in the hearts.

755
00:56:39,730 --> 00:56:42,030
If a person has doubts in their hearts.

756
00:56:43,462 --> 00:56:48,419
It is not the sin but it is, it can lead to disbelieving in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

757
00:56:48,495 --> 00:56:49,736
so it's not an easy matter.

758
00:56:49,760 --> 00:56:52,490
I mean a person could be committing adultery, they could be drinking,

759
00:56:53,002 --> 00:56:56,197
they could be doing a lot of Haram(حرام)

760
00:56:56,222 --> 00:56:59,050
but they believe in Allah and His message, they have no doubts in them.

761
00:57:00,064 --> 00:57:03,988
However, a person could pretend to be a Muslim doing all of the Ibadaat(عبادات),

762
00:57:04,296 --> 00:57:06,077
but they have these doubts in their hearts

763
00:57:06,396 --> 00:57:08,807
and they could be counted among the camp of Al-Munafiqeen(ألمنافقين).

764
00:57:09,374 --> 00:57:11,763
So we need to be very, very careful when it comes to,

765
00:57:12,405 --> 00:57:15,867
where we stand on the issue of Sharia(شريعة)?

766
00:57:16,777 --> 00:57:20,556
Anything that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said, anything that Rasool Allah ﷺ said

767
00:57:20,581 --> 00:57:23,370
we need to take it and accept it as it is.

768
00:57:24,234 --> 00:57:26,976
And that is the whole point of being a Muslim,

769
00:57:27,024 --> 00:57:29,196
because the meaning of Islam we always say that

770
00:57:29,221 --> 00:57:32,285
the meaning of Islam is peace which is not correct.

771
00:57:32,439 --> 00:57:33,872
The meaning of Islam is Submission.

772
00:57:35,062 --> 00:57:37,222
Islam does not mean peace, Islam means submission.

773
00:57:38,148 --> 00:57:40,636
فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُ لِلْجَبِينِ

774
00:57:40,667 --> 00:57:42,730
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said about Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل).

775
00:57:43,039 --> 00:57:46,831
When Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was about to slaughter his son, he said: "أَسْلَمَا" They submitted.

776
00:57:47,612 --> 00:57:51,824
That is the fulfillment of the meaning of Islam.

777
00:57:53,199 --> 00:57:55,835
And the reason why Hajj(حَجْ) is such a great Ibadah(عبادة)

778
00:57:55,859 --> 00:57:59,921
is because it involves thing that you do, without knowing the reason why you're doing them.

779
00:58:01,260 --> 00:58:06,830
Why are you going around rock building made out of stone.?

780
00:58:07,953 --> 00:58:09,486
 Why do you kiss a stone.?

781
00:58:10,454 --> 00:58:13,021
So submission is very important.

782
00:58:13,366 --> 00:58:16,345
 A Muslim is not a Muslim without submitting to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

783
00:58:16,538 --> 00:58:19,053
You might not know the reason, you might not know the wisdom

784
00:58:19,078 --> 00:58:22,055
but you accept it, why because Allah said so.

785
00:58:22,872 --> 00:58:24,436
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ said so.

786
00:58:25,256 --> 00:58:27,914
So if I tell you about things that Rasool Allah ﷺ did

787
00:58:27,939 --> 00:58:29,715
and you just don't feel comfortable about them.

788
00:58:33,325 --> 00:58:34,259
What do you do?

789
00:58:34,831 --> 00:58:37,545
I tell you a story that Rasool Allah ﷺ did so and so.

790
00:58:37,763 --> 00:58:40,370
You just don't feel comfortable, you don't think that that's right,

791
00:58:40,395 --> 00:58:42,720
 but I tell you that this story is authentic, it's true,

792
00:58:44,222 --> 00:58:46,757
you doubt in your heart, you say there's something wrong with my heart

793
00:58:46,781 --> 00:58:48,826
there's something wrong with the way I see things.

794
00:58:50,011 --> 00:58:51,972
What Rasool Allah ﷺ did was right.

795
00:58:52,448 --> 00:58:54,976
And the reason why I don't like it is because I have a problem.

796
00:58:56,980 --> 00:58:58,177
That's how you should view it.

797
00:59:01,513 --> 00:59:04,723
Because there are going to be things in Shariah(شريعة) that you wouldn't understand

798
00:59:04,748 --> 00:59:12,116
and you might feel that, it doesn't sound right to me. Why?

799
00:59:12,140 --> 00:59:16,220
It doesn't sound right because Jahl(جهل), either because of ignorance,

800
00:59:16,788 --> 00:59:21,306
or because of a Fitrah(فطرة) that has been changed

801
00:59:21,369 --> 00:59:24,826
because the right Fitrah(فطرة) will not have a problem with anything in Shariah(شريعة).

802
00:59:25,393 --> 00:59:27,306
So you'd say that there's something wrong with my Fitrah(فطرة).

803
00:59:27,331 --> 00:59:28,842
I need to change it, I need to fix it.

804
00:59:33,769 --> 00:59:35,493
كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَكُمْ

805
00:59:35,543 --> 00:59:38,629
For example, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم they have experienced war

806
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:42,723
and some of them did not like it when it was prescribed on them, some of them felt uncomfortable,

807
00:59:42,911 --> 00:59:44,071
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told them;

808
00:59:44,347 --> 00:59:46,266
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تُحِبُّوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَكُمْ ۗ

809
00:59:46,328 --> 00:59:49,801
We might dislike something but there's a lot of good in it, for you.

810
00:59:50,280 --> 00:59:51,749
So good comes from Allah.

811
00:59:54,944 --> 00:59:59,366
Men marrying four women, a man marrying 100 women

812
00:59:59,391 --> 01:00:01,366
if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said so, than it's the right thing.

813
01:00:02,118 --> 01:00:06,998
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said that as soon as you reach the age of 20,

814
01:00:07,150 --> 01:00:11,609
you need to start standing for five hours a day on one foot, until you die.

815
01:00:12,127 --> 01:00:14,045
That would be the right thing, if Allah said so.

816
01:00:14,901 --> 01:00:18,332
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ doesn't order to do anything except if it's good,

817
01:00:18,684 --> 01:00:21,686
and He doesn't prevent us from doing anything, except that it is evil.

818
01:00:25,505 --> 01:00:28,911
We can talk about the Hikmah(حكمة), of how come a man was allowed to marry four women,

819
01:00:29,209 --> 01:00:30,471
while a woman was not.

820
01:00:31,121 --> 01:00:35,659
But Hikmah(حكمة) is irrelevant, we submit and we accept it.

821
01:00:37,538 --> 01:00:41,835
And I can't stress this point more because

822
01:00:41,901 --> 01:00:44,459
that is the first description Allah give to Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين).

823
01:00:45,347 --> 01:00:48,146
هُدًى لِلْمُتَّقِينَ ۝ الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ

824
01:00:49,925 --> 01:00:53,269
 Qur'an is guidance for the Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين), the pious ones,

825
01:00:53,363 --> 01:00:54,079
who are they?

826
01:00:54,262 --> 01:00:56,230
The ones, who believe in the unseen.

827
01:00:57,254 --> 01:00:59,012
They believe in things that they never saw.

828
01:00:59,827 --> 01:01:02,789
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: It wouldn't make a difference for me

829
01:01:02,814 --> 01:01:06,781
if I see Jannah(جنة) in front of my eyes or if I see Hellfire in front of my eyes

830
01:01:06,984 --> 01:01:10,221
because I have Yaqeen(يقين) it can't make a difference if I see it.

831
01:01:10,721 --> 01:01:12,083
I'm not gonna believe in it, more.

832
01:01:13,162 --> 01:01:14,400
That is Ilm-Ul-Yaqeen(علم اليقين)

833
01:01:15,323 --> 01:01:16,488
that is certain faith.

834
01:01:16,718 --> 01:01:18,630
That's what we need to have, that is Islam.

835
01:01:19,394 --> 01:01:22,280
It's alright, it's fine to look for the wisdom and the Hikmah(حكمة).

836
01:01:22,810 --> 01:01:28,853
However, should not hold back on believing, until you understand the meaning,

837
01:01:30,044 --> 01:01:33,195
otherwise it's gonna be just like any other empirical experiment

838
01:01:33,925 --> 01:01:37,560
you prove it scientifically and it becomes logic.

839
01:01:38,413 --> 01:01:41,412
So where is element of faith, where is the element of Eeman(ايمان).

840
01:01:42,234 --> 01:01:43,691
Where is Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ testing you.

841
01:01:44,562 --> 01:01:50,663
Is it permissible to abstain from marriage in order to be able to be like the Sahabah(صحابه),

842
01:01:50,991 --> 01:01:54,060
to free oneself from having to stay behind and care for one spouse.

843
01:01:55,705 --> 01:01:59,344
You know a person is not allowed to take a vow of celibacy

844
01:01:59,384 --> 01:02:01,786
that is Rahbaniyyah(رهبانية) that is not allowed in Islam,

845
01:02:02,400 --> 01:02:05,456
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tested the Sahabah(صحابه) through their wives and children.

846
01:02:07,184 --> 01:02:10,801
They got married and they had children, and that was a test for them,

847
01:02:11,152 --> 01:02:13,703
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told the ones, who failed in the test,

848
01:02:14,348 --> 01:02:17,502
إِنَّ مِنْ أَزْوَاجِكُمْ وَأَوْلَادِكُمْ عَدُوًّا لَكُمْ فَاحْذَرُوهُمْ ۚ

849
01:02:19,011 --> 01:02:21,574
Some of them stayed behind and they did not make Hijrah(هجرة).

850
01:02:22,403 --> 01:02:29,537
So later on when Makkah was opened and Islam dominated.

851
01:02:30,838 --> 01:02:33,417
They will go back to their wives and children and blame them,

852
01:02:34,042 --> 01:02:36,634
and say it's just because of you, we didn't make Hijrah(هجرة) early.

853
01:02:38,030 --> 01:02:39,090
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told them,

854
01:02:39,159 --> 01:02:44,181
إِنَّ مِنْ أَزْوَاجِكُمْ وَأَوْلَادِكُمْ عَدُوًّا لَكُمْ فَاحْذَرُوهُمْ

855
01:02:44,854 --> 01:02:48,332
From among your wives and children are enemies for you so beware.

856
01:02:48,854 --> 01:02:52,170
وَإِنْ تَعْفُوا وَتَصْفَحُوا وَتَغْفِرُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

857
01:02:52,777 --> 01:02:58,299
But if you are forgiving Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is forgiving, Merciful.

858
01:02:58,323 --> 01:03:00,254
Now, it's too late to blame them, forgive them.

859
01:03:01,328 --> 01:03:04,757
Now, you're opening up the blame game and saying it was because of you.

860
01:03:04,782 --> 01:03:06,814
We missed Jihad(جهاد) and we missed Hijrah(هجرة).

861
01:03:07,053 --> 01:03:08,035
No! Forgive them,

862
01:03:08,059 --> 01:03:09,430
وَإِنْ تَعْفُوا وَتَصْفَحُوا وَتَغْفِرُوا

863
01:03:10,028 --> 01:03:13,883
You should have made that decision to make a move early on, so get married,

864
01:03:14,848 --> 01:03:18,629
if you have some conditions to your wife make those conditions before you get married,

865
01:03:20,689 --> 01:03:28,298
and try to find a companion who is like minded and is willing to help you in what you do.

866
01:03:29,626 --> 01:03:33,998
And the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

867
01:03:35,779 --> 01:03:40,166
 in fact Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he sent in his Waseea(وصية) before he died.

868
01:03:40,881 --> 01:03:46,023
He said: And don't hold back the soldiers from going back to their families,

869
01:03:46,347 --> 01:03:48,807
otherwise the progeny of the Muslims will end.

870
01:03:51,362 --> 01:03:55,166
So, the objective of marriage is, for Islam to carry on.

871
01:03:55,778 --> 01:03:57,724
And we said that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would say that

872
01:03:57,786 --> 01:04:03,074
sometimes he would force himself to sleep with his wife and he would say the reason is

873
01:04:03,755 --> 01:04:07,849
because Allah may create a soul that will make Tasbeeh(تسبيح) of Allah.

874
01:04:11,109 --> 01:04:16,287
So marriage has objectives and you have some objectives in life, bringing them together.

875
01:04:18,738 --> 01:04:21,618
Are we allowed to wear contact lenses men plus women?

876
01:04:22,039 --> 01:04:27,565
Medical reasons. Yes! If it's for, if it's those colored lenses.

877
01:04:29,390 --> 01:04:32,053
Than that would not be allowed, Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم).

878
01:04:33,651 --> 01:04:36,774
Is it permissible to perform Wadhoo(وضؤ), ablution with cotton socks?

879
01:04:37,268 --> 01:04:41,994
Anything that has thickness and covers the foot and covers the whole foot,

880
01:04:42,518 --> 01:04:45,826
including the ankles, can be used for a Masseh(مسح).

881
01:04:47,784 --> 01:04:50,888
I have prayed on and off until I was about 23 years old.

882
01:04:51,487 --> 01:04:55,936
That's why I started doing all the five prayers, do I have to make up for Missed Salah(صلاة)?

883
01:04:56,768 --> 01:05:00,069
The Scholars say nothing can make up for a missed Salah(صلاة).

884
01:05:00,675 --> 01:05:03,768
Miss Salah(صلاة) that was missed intentionally without an excuse,

885
01:05:03,886 --> 01:05:05,202
 nothing can make up for it.

886
01:05:06,117 --> 01:05:09,807
Just like missing a day of Ramadan(رمضان) without an excuse Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

887
01:05:09,914 --> 01:05:11,842
لم يَقضِ عنه صيامُ الدَّهرِ

888
01:05:12,632 --> 01:05:16,310
If he fast for an entire year, it would not make up for that day.

889
01:05:17,369 --> 01:05:22,486
So if you missed us a Salah(صلاة), nothing can make up for it, except a Taubah(توبة),

890
01:05:23,783 --> 01:05:26,811
a strong Taubah(توبة), a Taubah(توبة) of regret,

891
01:05:27,107 --> 01:05:30,244
because the most important pillar of Taubah(توبة) is regret.

892
01:05:30,335 --> 01:05:31,531
إنَّما التوبة النِدم

893
01:05:31,996 --> 01:05:33,276
"Taubah(توبة) is regret."

894
